Translation patch: `ParseBuf::eat_*` (whole-width integers and floats)

Change: The first arm of `eat_num!` takes the byte size as a literal (`eat_num!(eat_u16_le, checked_eat_u16_le, 2, u16::from_le_bytes)`) instead of computing `std::mem::size_of::<$t>()`.
Why: `core::mem::size_of` is not modelled by Aeneas (it cannot be defined in Lean).
Behaviour: Identical: the compiler checks the literal, since `$t::$fn` only accepts a `[u8; size_of::<$t>()]` array.

